Hotspot - a desktop controller for WPSD hotspots
================================================

Hotspot lets you watch and control a digital voice hotspot running WPSD
(the Pi-Star successor) from the RISC OS desktop. It talks to the hotspot's
own web dashboard over your network; nothing is installed on the hotspot.

Getting started
---------------
1. Double-click !Hotspot. An icon appears on the icon bar.
2. Click it (Select) to open the window. The first time, the Choices window
   opens: check the hotspot's IP address (10.0.0.27 to begin with), and type
   the password for its Admin pages (the user name is normally pi-star).
   Click Save. Tab, or Return, moves from one box to the next.
3. The window fills in. The tabs along the top switch between:

     Status   radio state, modes and networks, with Pause/Resume buttons
     Heard    the last heard list; a live transmission is highlighted
     DMR      switch DMR networks (BrandMeister, TGIF) on and off, manage
              BrandMeister talkgroups, link TGIF talkgroups
     YSF      the hotspot's list of YSF reflectors and FCS rooms: search it
              by part of a name, number or place and click Link
     Links    link or unlink YSF, D-Star, P25, NXDN reflectors/talkgroups;
              the last few you used are one click away
     System   restart services, update host files, reboot, shut down

The Menu button over the window gives the same actions as a menu; the Menu
button over the icon bar icon gives Info (move the pointer onto its arrow for
the Program information window), Help (this file), Find hotspot, Choices and
Quit. (Clicking the icon bar icon opens the window.)
F5 refreshes (click in the window first so it receives the key).

If the hotspot's address changes
--------------------------------
The address can change when the router hands out a new one. Click Find
hotspot... (in the window, either menu, or beside the "Not connected"
message), check the first three numbers of your network's addresses, and
click Search. Every address from 1 to 254 is tried. Each hotspot found is
offered to you: click Continue to use it. Choices has the address too, to type in.
Giving the hotspot a fixed address in your router avoids all this.

What needs a login
------------------
Looking is free: the status, last heard and radio information are public on
the dashboard. Everything that changes something (and the DMR network and
BrandMeister lists) uses the Admin login you entered in Choices. If the
login is wrong the window says so.

If something does not work
--------------------------
System > Save diagnostics writes a report (what was asked of the hotspot and
what it answered, without the password) next to the Choices file. Send that
report along with a description of what you expected.
